  "binding": "current",
  "outcome": "partial",
  "summary": "Phase 1a of the occurrence-host plan repaired the built autocomplete owner in the working tree; Phases 1b, 2 and 3 have not run. A completion now refuses a match offered by an earlier query even when a newer query has the same text, closing a law-6 gap where the owner compared text alone. While a typed trigger's query is open the editor root takes role combobox with aria-expanded, aria-haspopup and aria-autocomplete, drops aria-multiline, and gets back its earlier attribute values, or the app's later ones, when the query closes. Plate's shortcut table skips key events that report isComposing or carry keyCode 229, the code WebKit sends for an IME-confirming Enter, and plugin onKeyDown handlers still receive them. Trigger and query reads are bounded in characters, and Plite's editor.read.text.string copies only the requested part of a leaf, so an idle keystroke, a trigger and an open query cost 6, 7 and 3 characters at 2,000, 20,000 and 200,000-character paragraphs where HEAD cost up to 400,009.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "partial",
