        "claim": "Chromium's accessibility tree on /blocks/mention-demo shows the root as a multiline textbox before, a combobox that is expanded with a listbox popup and the active option Biggs Darklighter while a query is open, and a multiline textbox again after Escape."
      },
      {
        "path": "apps/www/tests/browser/combobox.spec.ts",
        "sha256": "efc2640f92ece4af4aa2b1b749f54b164d22198d6774da95404651eac82723bf",
        "claim": "With multi-editor.spec.ts, five warm repeats without retries on one development server: Chromium 110 passed, Firefox 100 passed and 10 skipped, WebKit 100 passed and 10 skipped; the mention case asserts an expanded combobox role while the popup shows."
      },
      {
        "path": "apps/www/scripts/run-combobox-typing-probe.mts",
        "sha256": "69390da94d97f7bc56b0463682065fcedc03f20b424f6e3b3457eff056b324c3",
        "claim": "The frozen key-to-paint contract, five runs of 100 keys paced 100 ms at 2,000 characters on the development server: kits on p95 11.2 ms against kits off 10.5 ms, +0.7 ms and +6.7 percent, inside the 10 percent and 1 ms budget."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Run logs are local under docs/plans/artifacts/2026-10-03-autocomplete-occurrence-host/phase-1a-acceptance, which is git-ignored; a matching hash establishes identity, not a run. The final runs used a working checkout at HEAD fe0e9599a6 that held other sessions' uncommitted edits; the acceptance summary records the hashes of the eight files this phase changed. No screen reader has run; Chromium's accessibility tree is the strongest recognition proof, and it does not list aria-autocomplete. WebKit's confirming Enter on a real IME is unproven, and IME proof is Chromium CDP composition only. The key-to-paint contract ran on the development server; the plan's calibrated production-build benchmark with an A/A pairing and a known-bad candidate has not run. Phase 1b's typed-text report and textToCaret, Phase 2's host and Phase 3's screen-reader runs are not built. The string-data paste, yank, drop and replacement typing-check violation of hard law 5 and the Android keyboard-clipboard paste remain open."
